  "summary": "<table><thead><tr><th>Methodology Step #</th><th>Official CompTIA Step Name</th><th>Primary Technical Objective</th><th>Key Distinguishing Exam Triggers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Step 1</strong></td><td><strong>Identify the Problem</strong></td><td>Gather info, question users (open-ended), duplicate issue, determine scope &amp; location, identify recent changes.</td><td>\"First step\", \"Questioning users\", \"Describe what you were doing\", \"Location and scope\", \"What changed?\"</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Step 2</strong></td><td><strong>Establish a Theory of Probable Cause</strong></td><td>Formulate hypotheses based on symptoms, question the obvious, leverage OSI layer models.</td><td>\"Question the obvious\", \"Consider top-down/bottom-up\", \"Formulate hypotheses\"</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Step 3</strong></td><td><strong>Test the Theory to Determine Cause</strong></td><td>Empirically test theories one by one. If disproven, re-establish new theory.</td><td>\"Test each cause\", \"Diagnosed symptoms and know likely cause\", \"Divide-and-Conquer ping\"</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Step 4</strong></td><td><strong>Establish a Plan of Action</strong></td><td>Design repair steps, evaluate potential side effects/disruptions, build rollback plan, schedule maintenance window.</td><td>\"Plan of action\", \"Schedule disruption\", \"Notify users\", \"Identify potential side effects\"</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Step 5</strong></td><td><strong>Implement Solution or Escalate</strong></td><td>Execute technical repair during scheduled window OR perform warm handoff to higher tier with established facts.</td><td>\"Next step after Plan\", \"Replacing faulty switch\", \"Warm handoff\", \"Communicate basic facts\"</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Step 6</strong></td><td><strong>Verify Full System Functionality</strong></td><td>Validate primary fix with end user, ensure overall system functionality unaffected, implement <strong>preventive measures</strong>.</td><td>\"Check user workflow\", \"Preventive measures\", \"Validate fix without affecting overall system\"</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Step 7</strong></td><td><strong>Document Findings, Actions, &amp; Outcomes</strong></td><td>Log complete incident history in ticketing system/Knowledge Base (KB), close ticket.</td><td>\"Last step\", \"Final step\", \"Knowledge base\", \"Log findings, actions, and outcomes\"</td></tr></tbody></table>",
  "checklist": "<ul><li>[ ] <strong>CompTIA 7-Step Sequence Mastery:</strong> Can you list all 7 steps of the CompTIA troubleshooting framework in exact numerical order without hesitation?</li><li>[ ] <strong>Process Transition Recognition:</strong> Given any troubleshooting scenario (e.g., \"Plan complete\", \"Theory confirmed\", \"Fix applied\"), can you instantly identify the exact next step?</li><li>[ ] <strong>User Interviewing Techniques:</strong> Do you understand why open-ended questions (\"Describe what you were doing...\") are superior to closed-ended questions when interviewing non-technical users?</li><li>[ ] <strong>Diagnostic Questions:</strong> Can you identify \"Did it ever work?\" and \"What has changed since it last worked?\" as the two primary root cause discovery questions?</li><li>[ ] <strong>Scope and Location Triangulation:</strong> Do you know how determining problem location isolates the <em>source</em>, while determining scope isolates <em>priority/severity</em>?</li><li>[ ] <strong>OSI Troubleshooting Approaches:</strong></li><ul><li>[ ] <em>Bottom-Up:</em> Starts at Layer 1 (Physical cables, NICs, link lights).</li><li>[ ] <em>Top-Down:</em> Starts at Layer 7 (User application, browser settings).</li><li>[ ] <em>Divide-and-Conquer:</em> Starts in the middle (Layer 3/4 ping/traceroute) and moves UP or DOWN based on test results.</li></ul><li>[ ] <strong>Multiple Simultaneous Problems:</strong> Do you understand why multiple symptoms must always be decomposed and treated as <em>separate individual cases</em>?</li><li>[ ] <strong>Escalation Requirements:</strong> Can you identify that establishing basic facts and communicating those facts clearly during a warm handoff are mandatory prerequisites before escalating a ticket?</li><li>[ ] <strong>Disruptive Change Management:</strong> Do you know that disruptive fixes mandate scheduling an off-peak maintenance window and sending advance notifications to affected users?</li><li>[ ] <strong>Verification Objectives:</strong> Do you understand that Step 6 requires verifying the fix with the end user, ensuring overall system stability, AND implementing preventive measures?</li><li>[ ] <strong>Documentation Finality:</strong> Can you explain why logging Findings, Actions, and Outcomes in a Knowledge Base (KB) is strictly required as the final step before ticket closure?</li></ul>"
